  "content": {
    "id": "p13-evaluate-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Evaluate.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-evaluate-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt[2]{1}\\times\\sqrt[4]{2}\\times\\sqrt[8]{4}\\times\\sqrt[16]{8}\\times\\sqrt[32]{16}\\times\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2$.\n\nConvert to base $2$; the exponent sum is $1$.",
          "worked": "Let $P$ be the product. Converting the radicals to powers of $2$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}P&=2^{1/4}\\times2^{2/8}\\times2^{3/16}\\times\\cdots\\\\P&=2^x,\\end{align*}$$\nwhere $x=\\frac14+\\frac28+\\frac3{16}+\\cdots$. This convergent series satisfies\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac x2&=\\frac18+\\frac2{16}+\\frac3{32}+\\cdots\\\\x-\\frac x2&=\\frac14+\\frac18+\\frac1{16}+\\cdots\\\\\\frac x2&=\\frac{1/4}{1-1/2}\\\\\\frac x2&=\\frac12\\\\x&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $P=2^1=2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 106
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-evaluate-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt[1]{1}\\times\\sqrt[2]{2}\\times\\sqrt[4]{4}\\times\\sqrt[8]{8}\\times\\sqrt[16]{16}\\times\\cdots$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4$.\n\nEach factor is the square of the corresponding factor in part a, so the product is $2^2$.",
          "worked": "Let $Q$ be this product and $P$ the product in part a. Each root index has been halved, so each factor has been squared. Applying this to finite partial products and then taking their limits gives\n$$\\begin{align*}Q&=P^2\\\\Q&=2^2\\\\Q&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 76
      }
    ]
  },
